# Targets to delete from the home directory, not just stop managing. Chezmoi
# leaves a deployed file in place when its source is removed, so a deletion in
# the source tree alone would strand these on any machine that already applied
# them.
#
# Both were part of the mcp-init scaffolding: base-servers.json declared MCP
# servers for a per-project .mcp.json that merge-claude-config.sh generated.
# Claude Code never read either one (it reads ~/.claude.json), the mechanism
# produced no .mcp.json anywhere in three months, and base-servers.json passed
# an API key as a --api-key command-line argument, which is visible in `ps` to
# anything running as this user. See CLAUDE.md "Secrets".
#
# Safe to delete this whole file once both Macs have applied it once.
.config/mcp/base-servers.json
.config/scripts/merge-claude-config.sh
